  "title": "Vowels 1b: ই ঈ",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**ই** and **ঈ** are both `i` as in *see*. Their names are 'short i' (ই) and 'long i' (ঈ), but **in everyday speech they sound the same**. You just learn which one each word is spelled with:\n\n- **ই**লিশ (hilsa), **ই**ট (brick)\n- **ঈ**গল (eagle), **ঈ**দ (Eid)\n\nBecause they sound alike, you will only ever tell them apart by sight, never by ear.\n\n*Culture:* ইলিশ is Bangladesh's national fish, and ঈদ is one of the biggest holidays of the year.",
  "vocab": [
